                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "number": 7,
                    "title": "RESULT",
                    "text": [
                        "The CMOS inverter repeater was successfully designed and simulated in 180 nm technology. Repeater insertion reduced the average propagation delay from approximately 3.00 ns to 1.20 ns, showing that repeaters significantly improve the speed of circuits driving large interconnects"
                    ]
